  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Workshop on Strategic Environmental Assessment in Morocco&apos;s hydrogen sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supports a workshop to strengthen Moroccan institutional capacity on Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) in the context of green hydrogen development.As Morocco advances its &quot;Offre Maroc&quot; and selects flagship hydrogen projects, the workshop addresses the need to better anticipate cumulative environmental and social impacts and integrate sustainability into long term planning.The workshop is organised by the Netherlands Commission for Environmental Assessment in collaboration with the Ministry of Energy Transition and Sustainable Development. It introduces SEA tools, shares international experience and explores how SEA can support Morocco&apos;s hydrogen planning, with a follow up session to identify possible next steps. CERF funding supports logistical aspects of the event, including the venue, catering and interpretation.</narrative>
  </description>
